</span></span><span><span></span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(204, 123, 244);">FROM</span><span> STATION
</span></span><span><span></span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(204, 123, 244);">WHERE</span><span> CITY </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(234, 236, 240);">NOT</span><span> </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(234, 236, 240);">REGEXP</span><span> </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">'^[AEIOUaeiou].*[AEIOUaeiou]$'</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">;</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>What this does:</strong> Returns all cities that do <strong>not</strong> start AND end with a vowel (both conditions must fail together).</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>Breaking down the REGEXP:</strong></p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto w-full px-2 mb-6"><table class="min-w-full border-collapse text-sm leading-[1.7] whitespace-normal"><thead class="text-left"><tr><th scope="col" class="text-text-100 border-b-0.5 border-border-300/60 py-2 pr-4 align-top font-bold">Part</th><th scope="col" class="text-text-100 border-b-0.5 border-border-300/60 py-2 pr-4 align-top font-bold">Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top"><code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">^</code></td><td class="border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Start of string</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top"><code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">[AEIOUaeiou]</code></td><td class="border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Starts with a vowel (case-insensitive)</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top"><code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">.*</code></td><td class="border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Any characters in between</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top"><code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">[AEIOUaeiou]</code></td><td class="border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Ends with a vowel</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top"><code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">$</code></td><td class="border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top">End of string</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">The <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">NOT</code> negates the whole pattern — so it returns cities where it's <strong>not true</strong> that they both start and end with a vowel.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>Why your original query may be wrong:</strong></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Your version used <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">^[AEIOU]</code> (uppercase only), which would <strong>miss lowercase vowels</strong>. Always include both cases: <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">[AEIOUaeiou]</code>, or use <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">REGEXP_LIKE</code> with the <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">'i'</code> flag in some databases.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>Alternative using <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">RLIKE</code> (same as REGEXP in MySQL):</strong></p>
